# RailEats Hero Slider CMS

## SQL Table

The feature uses the existing Supabase table:

```sql
public.hero_slider
- id bigint identity primary key
- title text
- image_url text not null
- sort_order integer default 1
- active boolean default true
- created_at timestamptz default now()
```

## Storage Bucket

The feature uses the existing Supabase Storage bucket:

```txt
hero-slider
```

Uploaded files are stored under:

```txt
hero-slider/homepage/
```

## Files Created

```txt
app/admin/website/hero-slider/page.tsx
components/admin/HeroSliderManager.tsx
app/api/admin/hero-slider/route.ts
app/api/hero-slider/route.ts
components/HeroSlider.tsx
```

## How Admin Uploads Image

1. Open Admin page:

```txt
/admin/website/hero-slider
```

2. Select a JPG, PNG or WebP image.
3. Enter optional title.
4. Set sort order.
5. Choose active or inactive.
6. Click Save Slider.

The admin API uploads the image to Supabase Storage bucket `hero-slider`, creates a public URL, and inserts the record into `public.hero_slider`.

Editing a slider can update title, order, active status, and optionally replace the image.

Deleting a slider removes the database row and also tries to remove the uploaded storage image.

## How Homepage Fetches Slider

The public frontend component `components/HeroSlider.tsx` fetches:

```txt
/api/hero-slider
```

That API returns only active sliders ordered by `sort_order` ascending:

```txt
id
title
image_url
sort_order
```

If there are no active sliders or the API fails, the component uses fallback images:

```txt
/slides/happy-new-year.png
/slides/offer50.png
/slides/offer20.png
/slides/offer-combo.png
/slides/hot-fresh.png
```

Recommended uploaded image size:

```txt
1600 x 900 px
```
